codex
The one-GEMM trial failed because the existing Triton kernels assume each projection is stored as a separate contiguous `[pairs,H]` tensor; split views from a packed `[pairs,5H]` projection have a larger row stride. I’m testing stride-aware packed kernels now, which keeps the potential GEMM win without corrupting the layout.
